** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cotyledon.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌkɑt.əˈliː.dən/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːdən|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|physiology}} Each of the patches of [[villi]] on the [[foetal]] [[chorion]] in the [[placenta]] of [[ruminant]]s and some other mammals.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1997|author=w:Roy Porter|title=The Greatest Benefit to Mankind|page=72|publisher=Folio Society|year_published=2016
|passage=Forced to apply animal findings to humans, his human womb also had '''cotyledons''' like a dog's.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q193026}}{{lb|en|botany}} The [[leaf]] of the [[embryo]] of a [[seed]]-[[bearing]] [[plant]]; after [[germination]] it becomes the first leaves of the [[seedling]].

